    "note": [
        {
            "structuredValue": [],
            "parallelValue": [],
            "groupedValue": [],
            "value": "There are two datasets here, both involving Uzbek grammaticality judgments for different types of sluicing-like constructions and cleft sentences. \r\n\r\nThe survey file (SLC-cleft) records the responses 12 of 14 total participants. 10 of the 12 listed speakers were located in Uzbekistan at the time of data collection. Note the co-variation w.r.t. accusative case marking on pivots of copular and cleft sentences, as well as remnants of sluicing-like constructions.\r\n\r\nThe file called \"clefts\" records the judgments of one speaker only.\r\n\r\nThese findings, and the analysis, are reported in the following paper: \r\n\r\nGribanova, Vera. Copular clauses, clefts, and putative sluicing in Uzbek. Language 89(4): 830–882. [http://muse.jhu.edu/article/532706]",
            "type": "abstract",
            "identifier": [],
            "note": [],
            "appliesTo": []
        },
